{
  "_comment": "The Script of Rhys, plain register (design_v2 §11). Glyph shapes transcribed from script.xcf and cleaned up; redesigning a glyph is an edit here, nothing else (§11.9). Read by game/script/rhys_script.gd; docs/authoring/script.md explains every field. Missing keys are hard errors.",

  "_grid_comment": "Glyph coordinates are in grid units: y runs 0 (top of the slot) to grid (bottom). x starts at 0 on the glyph's left and runs to w. A stroke is a polyline [x0,y0, x1,y1, ...]. Full-height glyphs map grid units to (height_px - 1) / grid pixels, so heights of 12k+1 (13, 25, 37) land every grid point on a whole pixel.",
  "grid": 12,

  "_layout_comment": "In grid units of the full slot. slot_gap: blank columns between slots. cluster_gap: blank rows between the two halves of a stacked slot (each half gets what is left, halved). line_gap: blank rows between lines. All four are placeholders, not decided design.",
  "layout": {
    "slot_gap": 3,
    "cluster_gap": 1,
    "line_gap": 6,
    "padding_px": 1
  },

  "_render_comment": "Defaults for the bake tool and the ScriptText node when they are not given a value. ink is RRGGBB or RRGGBBAA.",
  "render": {
    "height_px": 25,
    "stroke_px": 1,
    "ink": "000000"
  },

  "_glyphs_comment": "class: consonant | vowel | null | space. input: what you type for it (lower case; longest match wins, '.' or '·' splits a digraph). pair_of: the consonant this one is built on with a base stroke (§11.2) — information only. The ids 'null' (' and |) and '_' (underscore space) are fixed; every other id is also how the glyph prints in a chain.",
